      "title": "San Francisco State University - Details - Project Coordinator-Housing Capital & Life Safety- (Housing Operations Professional III, Range 1) - HDCS Housing, Dining and Conference Services",
      "description": "San Francisco State University - Details - Project Coordinator-Housing Capital & Life Safety- (Housing Operations Professional III, Range 1) - HDCS Housing, Dining and Conference Services Skip to main content SAN FRANCISCO STATE UNIVERSITY | Human Resources A–Z Calendar Login Search\n                                        SF State Search SF State Button SF State This Site Toggle navigation Menu Main navigation What's New Get Started Expand Future Employees New Employees Current Employees HR Liaisons Managers Students Jobs Benefits & Retirement Expand Overview Medical Benefits Dental Benefits Vision Benefits Retirement Services Employee Assistance Program Fee Waiver Program Voluntary Benefits & Discounts Payroll Expand Overview Payroll & Paycheck Essentials Payroll Calendar & Schedules Employment Verification Leave Accrual and Absence Management Resources Cal Employee Connect Employee Separation Clearance Process Classification & Compensation Learning & Development Expand Professional Development Performance Management Process CSU Learn Labor Relations Compliance Expand Overview Whistleblower Leaves/ Employee Accommodations/Workers' Comp Expand Leaves Program Employee Accommodations Services Workers' Compensation Resources Expand COVID-19 Employee Life Events Employee Resource Groups HR Events / Training Staff Years of Service Recognition Workplace Resources Immigration Resources CSU International Travel Expand CSU International Travel Resources CSU International Travel Guidance for Spring & Summer 2025 Community Expectations ADA: 504 and Title II Policies and Procedures Expand Policies & Procedures (Main) All Employees Faculty Management Personnel & Confidential Staff (Represented / Non-Represented) Student Employees Job Opportunities Applicant Login Job Search Filter Results Work type Staff 1 Locations Northern California San Francisco 1 Categories Appointment Type Probationary 1 Bargaining Unit Unit 9 - CSUEU - Technical Support Services 1 Job Search Category/Discipline Administrative 1 Time Basis Full Time 1 Workplace Type (Exclude Inst Fac) On-site (work in-person at business location) 1 Project Coordinator-Housing Capital & Life Safety- (Housing Operations Professional III, Range 1) - HDCS Housing, Dining and Conference Services Apply now Job no: 560429 Work type: Staff Location: San Francisco Categories: Unit 9 - CSUEU - Technical Support Services, Administrative, Probationary, Full Time, On-site (work in-person at business location) *SFSU INTERNAL APPLICANTS ONLY* Working Title Project Coordinator-Housing Capital & Life Safety Positions Available 1 SF State University San Francisco State is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate against persons on the basis of race, religion, color, ancestry, age, disability, genetic information, gender, gender identity, gender expression, marital status, medical condition, National origin, sex, sexual orientation, covered veteran status, or any other protected status.  Reasonable accommodations will be provided for qualified applicants with disabilities who self-disclose by contacting the Senior Human Resources Manager. Applicants may visit titleix.sfsu.edu for more information on SF State's policy prohibiting discrimination, and how to file an online report using the procedures under Executive Order 1096 Revised. Inquiries can be directed to the campus Title IX Coordinator and Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Administrator by calling (415) 338-2032 or emailing vpsaem@sfsu.edu. San Francisco State is a 100% Smoke/Vapor-Free Campus.  Smoking or Vaping of any tobacco/plant-based substance is not permitted on any University properties. The person holding this position may be considered a \"mandated reporter\" under the California Child Abuse and Neglect  Reporting Act and is required to comply with the requirements set forth in CSU Executive Order 1083 as a condition of employment. This position may be a \"designated position\" in the California State University's Conflict of Interest Code.  The successful candidate accepting this position may be required to file Conflict of Interest forms subject to the regulations of the Fair Political Practices Commission. Department Housing, Dining & Conference Services Appointment Type This is a one-year probationary appointment. Time Base Full-Time (1.0 FTE) Work Schedule Monday-Friday 8:00 AM-5:00 PM Anticipated Hiring Range $5,079.00-6,315.00/monthly ($60,948–$75,780/annually) Salary is commensurate with experience. Position Summary Under the general direction of the Director of Housing Facilities (or designee), the Project Coordinator serves as a key professional responsible for planning, coordinating, and supporting housing-related capital improvement projects and Fire Life Safety (FLS) programs. The incumbent independently manages multiple projects of moderate to high scope and complexity, ensuring alignment with university standards, regulatory compliance, and operational priorities. This position acts as a liaison between Housing, Capital Planning Design & Construction (CPDC), Facilities Services, Environmental Health & Safety (EHS), contractors, and campus stakeholders. The role requires advanced project coordination, analytical, and communication skills to support project delivery, fire and life safety system compliance, and continuous improvement of housing operations. The incumbent exercises advanced judgment in coordinating complex projects, resolving issues, and ensuring compliance with regulatory and operational requirements, while ensuring projects meet scope, budget, and schedule expectations. Position Information Capital Planning, Design & Construction (CPDC) Project Coordination Coordinate housing capital projects from planning through execution, including renovations, deferred maintenance, and infrastructure improvements. Serve as primary liaison between Housing, CPDC, Facilities Services, and contractors to ensure project alignment with operational needs and timelines. Assist in project scoping, budgeting, scheduling, and documentation; track milestones and deliverables. Review project plans, drawings, and specifications to ensure compliance with housing operational standards. Coordinate project logistics including site access, resident communication, and stakeholder engagement. Monitor project progress and provide regular status reports; identify risks and recommend solutions. Support procurement processes, contractor coordination, and project closeout documentation. Utilize project management systems and CMMS tools to track work orders, projects, and performance metrics. Fire Life Safety (FLS) Program Coordination Coordinate fire and life safety programs within housing facilities, including fire alarm systems, suppression systems, inspections, and compliance activities. Assist in planning and managing preventative maintenance programs for fire and life safety systems. Track regulatory compliance with federal, state, CSU, and local fire and safety codes; coordinate inspections and corrective actions. Support budgeting, cost estimation, and prioritization of FLS projects and maintenance activities. Coordinate work performed by contractors and internal staff, ensuring adherence to safety standards and project requirements. Maintain documentation, records, and reporting related to life safety systems and compliance requirements. Partner with the Director of Business Operations and campus stakeholders, including EHS and Risk Management, to support emergency preparedness and response planning. Communicate system outages, impacts, and project updates to stakeholders and residents. Program Support and Analysis Analyze operational data, generate reports, and recommend process improvements for housing facilities and safety programs. Contribute to development and implementation of policies, procedures, and best practices related to housing operations. Evaluates and recommends improvements to policies, procedures, and operational practices to enhance efficiency, compliance, and service delivery. Evaluates and recommends improvements to policies, procedures, and operational practices to enhance efficiency, compliance, and service delivery. Evaluates and recommends improvements to policies, procedures, and operational practices to enhance efficiency, compliance, and service delivery. Evaluates and recommends improvements to policies, procedures, and operational practices to enhance efficiency, compliance, and service delivery. Evaluates and recommends improvements to policies, procedures, and operational practices to enhance efficiency, compliance, and service delivery. Provide lead work direction to student assistants or support staff as assigned. Participate in cross-functional teams, committees, and special projects. Other Duties as Assigned Minimum Qualifications Knowledge and Skill: Working skills and knowledge of housing operations including housing operations systems, policies, procedures, laws and regulations, and best practices. Working knowledge of student organizations, collegiate policies, and communications. Strong organizational skills to plan, organize, and prioritize multiple projects and large operations. Strong analytical skills to assess operational efficiency and support budget management. Ability to provide lead work direction and training to students and housing support staff. Strong communication and interpersonal skills to work effectively in a diverse environment and effectively gain buy-in from students and parents. Proficiency in using housing operations software and/or related equipment. Experience and Education: Equivalent to a bachelor's degree in a related field and two years of relevant experience. Additional experience which demonstrates acquired and successfully applied knowledge and abilities shown above may be substituted for the required education on a year-for-year basis. An advanced degree in a related field may be substituted for the required education on a year-for-year basis. Preferred Qualifications: Experience coordinating capital projects, construction, or facilities-related programs. Knowledge of Capital Planning, Design & Construction (CPDC) processes and project delivery methods. Experience with fire alarm systems, fire suppression systems, and/or fire life safety compliance programs. Knowledge of applicable building codes, fire/life safety regulations, and compliance requirements. Experience working in higher education, student housing, or institutional facilities environments. Ability to read and interpret construction drawings, specifications, and technical documents. Experience working with computerized maintenance management systems (CMMS) or project tracking tools. Experience coordinating contractors, vendors, and service providers. Coursework or certification in project management, facilities management, or related fields. Experience supporting emergency preparedness, safety programs, or risk management initiatives . Required License/Certification Must have a valid California Driver’s license (or ability to obtain within 30 days or hire). The person holding this position is considered a 'mandated reporter' under the California Child Abuse and Neglect Reporting Act and is required to comply with the requirements set forth in CSU Executive Order 1083 Revised July 21, 2017 as a condition of employment. Environmental/Physical/Special This position is fully in-person and on-site, requiring a regular physical presence on campus to support housing facilities, project coordination, and fire life safety operations. Work is performed in both office and field environments, including construction sites, mechanical spaces, and residential facilities. May be required to walk long distances, climb stairs, and access confined or restricted areas as part of project and facilities coordination. Must be able to respond to urgent or emergency situations, including after-hours support as needed. Participates in an on-call rotation and is expected to respond to emergencies and urgent operational needs outside of regular business hours. Work schedule may vary, including occasional evenings, weekends, and holidays to support project deadlines and operational needs. May be required to wear appropriate personal protective equipment (PPE) when working in active construction or maintenance environments. Pre-Employment Requirements: This position requires the successful completion of a background check. Eligibility to Work Applicants must be able to provide proof of US Citizenship or authorization to work in the United States, within three business days from their date of hire. Benefits Threaded through our Total Compensation package is a commitment to Bridging Life's Transitions.  SF State is committed to providing our employees with a comprehensive program that rewards efforts that are appreciated by your colleagues, students and the customers we serve. We offer a competitive compensation package that includes Medical, Dental, Vision, Pension, 401k, Healthcare Savings Account, Life Insurance, Disability Insurance, Vacation and Sick Leave as well as State Holidays and a dynamic Fee Waiver program, all geared towards the University's commitment to attract, motivate and retain our employee. CSUEU Position (For CSUEU Positions Only) Eligible and qualified on-campus applicants, currently in bargaining units 2, 5, 7, and 9 are given hiring preference. Additional Information SF STATE IS NOT A SPONSORING AGENCY FOR STAFF OR MANAGEMENT POSITIONS. (i.e. H1-B VISAS). Thank you for your interest in employment with California State University (CSU).  CSU is a state entity whose business operations reside within the State of California.  Because of this, CSU prohibits hiring employees to perform CSU-related work outside of California with very limited exception.  While this position may be eligible for occasional telework, all work is expected to be performed in the state of California, and this position is assigned to on-campus operations. CSU strongly encourages faculty, staff, and students who are accessing campus facilities to be immunized against COVID-19. The systemwide policy can be found at https://calstate.policystat.com/policy/9779821/latest/. The Human Resources office is open Mondays through Fridays from 8 a.m. to 5 p.m., and can be reached at (415) 338-1872. Please note that this position, position requirements, application deadline and/or any other component of this position is subject to change or cancellation at any time. *SFSU INTERNAL APPLICANTS ONLY* Advertised: September 01, 2026 (9:00 AM) Pacific Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Open Date Close Date Project Coordinator-Housing Capital & Life Safety- (Housing Operations Professional III, Range 1) - HDCS Housing, Dining and Conference Services San Francisco September 01, 2026 Under the general direction of the Director of Housing Facilities (or designee), the Project Coordinator serves as a key professional responsible for planning, coordinating, and supporting housing-related capital improvement projects and Fire Life Safety (FLS) programs. The incumbent independently manages multiple projects of moderate to high scope and complexity, ensuring alignment with university standards, regulatory compliance, and operational priorities. Current opportunities Position Location Open Date Close Date Project Coordinator-Housing Capital & Life Safety- (Housing Operations Professional III, Range 1) - HDCS Housing, Dining and Conference Services San Francisco September 01, 2026 Under the general direction of the Director of Housing Facilities (or designee), the Project Coordinator serves as a key professional responsible for planning, coordinating, and supporting housing-related capital improvement projects and Fire Life Safety (FLS) programs. The incumbent independently manages multiple projects of moderate to high scope and complexity, ensuring alignment with university standards, regulatory compliance, and operational priorities. Temporary Hiring Pools Loading... Powered by PageUp Contact Email: hrwww@sfsu.edu Telephone: 415.338.1872 / Fax: 415.338.0521 Need Assistance? Location San Francisco State University 1600 Holloway Avenue, ADM 252 San Francisco, CA 94132 Office Hours Monday through Friday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Quick Links HR Client Support Center Calendar & Schedules FAQ's Forms SF State Gateway Accessibility Equity & Community Inclusion Environment & Sustainability Privacy Policy Title IX San Francisco State\n                            University A\n                            California State University Campus SF State Facebook SF State Twitter SF State Instagram SF State LinkedIn"
