      "description": "San Francisco State University - Details - Network Engineer (Network and Communications Analyst IV, Range 1) - San Francisco Bay Region Network Skip to main content SAN FRANCISCO STATE UNIVERSITY | Human Resources A–Z Calendar Login Search\n                                        SF State Search SF State Button SF State This Site Toggle navigation Menu Main navigation What's New Get Started Expand Future Employees New Employees Current Employees HR Liaisons Managers Students Jobs Benefits & Retirement Expand Overview Medical Benefits Dental Benefits Vision Benefits Retirement Services Employee Assistance Program Fee Waiver Program Voluntary Benefits & Discounts Payroll Expand Overview Payroll & Paycheck Essentials Payroll Calendar & Schedules Employment Verification Leave Accrual and Absence Management Resources Cal Employee Connect Employee Separation Clearance Process Classification & Compensation Learning & Development Expand Professional Development Performance Management Process CSU Learn Labor Relations Compliance Expand Overview Whistleblower Leaves/ Employee Accommodations/Workers' Comp Expand Leaves Program Employee Accommodations Services Workers' Compensation Resources Expand COVID-19 Employee Life Events Employee Resource Groups HR Events / Training Staff Years of Service Recognition Workplace Resources Immigration Resources CSU International Travel Expand CSU International Travel Resources CSU International Travel Guidance for Spring & Summer 2025 Community Expectations ADA: 504 and Title II Policies and Procedures Expand Policies & Procedures (Main) All Employees Faculty Management Personnel & Confidential Staff (Represented / Non-Represented) Student Employees Job Opportunities Applicant Login Job Search Filter Results Work type Staff 1 Locations Northern California San Francisco 1 Categories Appointment Type Probationary 1 Bargaining Unit Unit 9 - CSUEU - Technical Support Services 1 Job Search Category/Discipline Information Systems & Technology 1 Time Basis Full Time 1 Network Engineer (Network and Communications Analyst IV, Range 1) - San Francisco Bay Region Network Apply now Job no: 561257 Work type: Staff Location: San Francisco Categories: Unit 9 - CSUEU - Technical Support Services, Probationary, Full Time, Information Systems & Technology **This position is open to applicants from SF State, CSU East Bay and Sonoma State Universities.** Working Title Network Engineer SF State University **The primary work location and designated home-campus for this role is SFSU** San Francisco State is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate against persons on the basis of race, religion, color, ancestry, age, disability, genetic information, gender, gender identity, gender expression, marital status, medical condition, National origin, sex, sexual orientation, covered veteran status, or any other protected status.  Reasonable accommodations will be provided for qualified applicants with disabilities who self-disclose by contacting the Senior Human Resources Manager. Applicants may visit titleix.sfsu.edu for more information on SF State's policy prohibiting discrimination, and how to file an online report using the procedures under Executive Order 1096 Revised. Inquiries can be directed to the campus Title IX Coordinator and Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Administrator by calling (415) 338-2032 or emailing vpsaem@sfsu.edu. San Francisco State is a 100% Smoke/Vapor-Free Campus.  Smoking or Vaping of any tobacco/plant-based substance is not permitted on any University properties. The person holding this position may be considered a \"mandated reporter\" under the California Child Abuse and Neglect  Reporting Act and is required to comply with the requirements set forth in CSU Executive Order 1083 as a condition of employment. This position may be a \"designated position\" in the California State University's Conflict of Interest Code.  The successful candidate accepting this position may be required to file Conflict of Interest forms subject to the regulations of the Fair Political Practices Commission. Department San Francisco Bay Region Network - Information Technology Services/Network and Telecommunications The San Francisco Bay Region Network (SFBRN) provides centralized administrative and transactional functions for CSUEB, SFSU, and SSU, creating a unified, cost-effective operational structure. The Information Technology Services (ITS) unit within the Network delivers secure, reliable, and innovative technology solutions that support all three universities. The unit manages infrastructure, application services, user support, information security, data management, and strategic IT operations. Partnering closely with each university’s leadership, including Presidents and Provosts, Information Technology Services drives digital transformation, promotes operational excellence, and supports institutional goals. Within ITS, the Network and Telecommunications Infrastructure team designs, implements, and supports the foundational technologies that connect the Network universities. The team oversees wired and wireless networks, f irewalls, switches, routers, VPNs, VoIP, and analog systems, ensuring secure, high-performance connectivity across academic, administrative, and residential environments. Through proactive management and modernization, the team strengthens the Network’s technological backbone, enabling seamless collaboration, teaching, research, and operations. Appointment Type This is a one-year probationary position. Time Base Full-time (1.0) Work Schedule Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Anticipated Hiring Range $8,231.00 - $10,647.00 Per Month ($98,772.00 - $127,764.00 Annually) Salary is commensurate with experience. Position Summary Reporting to and with minimal supervision from the Senior Director of Network and Telecommunications Infrastructure, the Network Engineer serves as a technical expert responsible for the planning, design, implementation, operation, and continuous improvement of enterprise network infrastructure across the San Francisco Bay Region Network, partner institutions, and auxiliary organizations. This position provides expert technical leadership for complex wired, wireless, remote access, and network management systems that support reliable, secure, scalable, and resilient connectivity across multiple universities. The Network Engineer leads highly complex network infrastructure initiatives and serves as a key technical advisor to management, technical teams, vendors, and campus stakeholders on enterprise network architecture, infrastructure modernization, service reliability, security, performance, and operational standards. The position develops technical strategies, architecture recommendations, standards, procedures, and best practices that guide the evolution of network services and ensure alignment with organizational priorities, regulatory requirements, and long-term service needs. The Network Engineer is responsible for evaluating, designing, deploying, administering, maintaining, and optimizing network hardware, configurations, monitoring platforms, security controls, and integrated communications technologies. Key duties include leading multi-site network design and deployment efforts, managing complex connectivity requirements, resolving unique and highly complex technical issues, analyzing capacity and performance trends, and recommending future-state improvements to support the organizational goals and long-term service needs of the San Francisco Bay Region Network. The role works collaboratively across technical, administrative, and institutional leadership groups to ensure consistent network security, service continuity, operational excellence, and effective delivery of enterprise network services. Position Information Enterprise Network Architecture, Program Management, and Infrastructure Leadership Plans, designs, implements, administers, maintains, and improves complex enterprise network infrastructure supporting the San Francisco Bay Region Network, partner institutions, and auxiliary organizations. Serves as a technical expert for wired, wireless, remote access, firewall, network management, monitoring, and related communications infrastructure supporting critical performance, scalability, security, and operational requirements. Coordinates and provides expert technical direction for highly complex network initiatives, including major upgrades, lifecycle replacements, new service deployments, modernization efforts, configuration changes, and multi-site improvements. Maintains expert technical stewardship of significant network architecture and infrastructure services supporting critical and high-impact operations across multiple universities and partner organizations. Develops and recommends network architecture strategies, technical standards, procedures, protocols, and best practices to improve scalability, resiliency, performance, security, and service delivery. Serves as a key technical advisor to management, technical teams, vendors, and campus stakeholders on complex network and communications solutions, infrastructure modernization, system integration, and service reliability. Evaluates networking technologies and service trends to recommend new and improved infrastructure solutions, future-state network improvements, operational enhancements, and long-term service needs. Provides expert technical direction in the resolution of highly complex and unique network infrastructure issues where precedents may not exist and where new approaches, procedures, or technical solutions may be required. Prepares technical analyses, architecture recommendations, implementation strategies, risk assessments, cost estimates, business justifications, and project documentation for major network initiatives. Provides technical oversight for the configuration, deployment, monitoring, lifecycle maintenance, and optimization of network hardware, systems, and services. Coordinates with technical teams, information security, vendors, consultants, facilities staff, and campus stakeholders to implement complex integrated network and communications solutions aligned with organizational priorities and approved technical direction Security, Compliance, and Administration Serves as a technical expert for network security administration, access controls, firewall policy management, secure remote access, vulnerability remediation, and related network protection practices. Develops, recommends, implements, and supports network security standards, procedures, protocols, and best practices to support secure, reliable, compliant, and resilient network services. Coordinates and provides expert technical direction for highly complex network security and administration initiatives, including firewall configuration reviews, access control improvements, patch management, vulnerability remediation, and configuration standardization. Provides technical guidance and recommendations to management, information security, technical teams, vendors, and campus stakeholders on network security, compliance requirements, risk mitigation, and operational controls. Administers and provides technical oversight for network management, monitoring, reporting, and configuration systems supporting operational requirements, compliance needs, incident response, and service reliability. Evaluates security alerts, vulnerability information, audit findings, configuration risks, and operational trends to recommend corrective actions, process improvements, and new or improved technical controls. Develops and maintains network documentation, configuration records, change records, diagrams, procedures, incident documentation, and service activity records to support audits, compliance, operational continuity, and knowledge transfer. Serves as a technical expert in the development, recommendation, and implementation of network governance practices, change-management procedures, and operational controls that support consistency, compliance, security, and service continuity across the Network and partner institutions. Network Performance, Optimization, and Continuous Improvement Serves as a technical expert for network performance monitoring, analytics, capacity planning, optimization, and service reliability across wired, wireless, remote access, and related communications infrastructure. Evaluates performance data, utilization trends, capacity requirements, service demands, and operational metrics to recommend improvements in efficiency, reliability, availability, resiliency, scalability, and service delivery. Provides expert technical direction for highly complex performance, capacity, availability, and service reliability issues, including root-cause analysis and recommendation of new or improved technical solutions. Develops and recommends performance standards, monitoring practices, reporting procedures, and operational improvements to proactively identify service risks, performance bottlenecks, and infrastructure constraints. Supports administration, monitoring, and optimization of unified communications platforms and integrated voice services where network performance, connectivity, quality of service, or service reliability are impacted. Evaluates call quality, network performance data, and integrated network-telecommunications requirements to recommend improvements that support reliable communications services. Provides technical analysis and recommendations for future-state network improvements, infrastructure planning, lifecycle management, and long-term service needs across the Network and partner institutions. Other Provides expert technical guidance, mentoring, training, and knowledge transfer to technical staff, project teams, and other technology professionals in support of complex network and communications initiatives. Contributes to promoting equity, diversity, and inclusion across the organization. Promotes the organization’s core values and consistently integrates innovation, employee fulfillment, teamwork, respect, excellence, integrity, service, and accountability into all aspects of work. Complies with Network, university, and unit policies and procedures regarding privacy of information, authorized use of Network resources, and the security of Network systems and data. Demonstrates safe work practices for oneself, others, and the office environment. Performs other related responsibilities as requested and when necessary. The Network reserves the right to add or change duties at any time. Minimum Qualifications Education and Experience: Equivalent to a bachelor’s degree in a related field and five years of relevant experience. Additional experience which demonstrates acquired and successfully applied knowledge and abilities shown above may be substituted for the required education on a year-for-year basis. An advanced degree in a related field may be substituted for the required experience on a year-for-year basis. Expert knowledge and understanding of network and communications administration, equipment, infrastructure, and related network and communications concepts, principles, and technologies. Expert knowledge and skill in applying and interpreting applicable standards, guidelines and, as appropriate, recommend new procedures, protocols, and standards. Expert analytical and organizational skills to organize, prioritize, and coordinate the successful completion of large, complex, and strategic network and communications development and improvement projects. Expert communication and interpersonal skills to effectively communicate complex technical systems and procedures as well as persuade stakeholders and management regarding system administration design and development options and procedures. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in higher education, multi-campus systems, or similarly complex public sector organizations. Environmental/Physical/Special Position may require travel among Network universities, as needed, to support operational and collaborative needs. This position may occasionally require work outside standard business hours to address emergencies and critical service needs. Pre-Employment Requirements This position requires the successful completion of a background check. Eligibility to Work Applicants must be able to provide proof of US Citizenship or authorization to work in the United States, within three business days from their date of hire. Benefits Threaded through our Total Compensation package is a commitment to Bridging Life's Transitions.  SF State is committed to providing our employees with a comprehensive program that rewards efforts that are appreciated by your colleagues, students and the customers we serve. We offer a competitive compensation package that includes Medical, Dental, Vision, Pension, 401k, Healthcare Savings Account, Life Insurance, Disability Insurance, Vacation and Sick Leave as well as State Holidays and a dynamic Fee Waiver program, all geared towards the University's commitment to attract, motivate and retain our employee. CSUEU Position (For CSUEU Positions Only) Eligible and qualified on-campus applicants, currently in bargaining units 2, 5, 7, and 9 are given hiring preference. Additional Information **This position is open to applicants from SF State, CSU East Bay and Sonoma State Universities.** SF STATE IS NOT A SPONSORING AGENCY FOR STAFF OR MANAGEMENT POSITIONS. (i.e. H1-B VISAS). Thank you for your interest in employment with California State University (CSU).  CSU is a state entity whose business operations reside within the State of California.  Because of this, CSU prohibits hiring employees to perform CSU-related work outside of California with very limited exception.  While this position may be eligible for occasional telework, all work is expected to be performed in the state of California, and this position is assigned to on-campus operations. CSU strongly encourages faculty, staff, and students who are accessing campus facilities to be immunized against COVID-19. The systemwide policy can be found at https://calstate.policystat.com/policy/9779821/latest/. The Human Resources office is open Mondays through Fridays from 8 a.m. to 5 p.m., and can be reached at (415) 338-1872. Please note that this position, position requirements, application deadline and/or any other component of this position is subject to change or cancellation at any time. Advertised: August 26, 2026 (9:00 AM) Pacific Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Open Date Close Date Network Engineer (Network and Communications Analyst IV, Range 1) - San Francisco Bay Region Network San Francisco August 26, 2026 The Network Engineer leads highly complex network infrastructure initiatives and serves as a key technical advisor to management, technical teams, vendors, and campus stakeholders on enterprise network architecture, infrastructure modernization, service reliability, security, performance, and operational standards. Current opportunities Position Location Open Date Close Date Network Engineer (Network and Communications Analyst IV, Range 1) - San Francisco Bay Region Network San Francisco August 26, 2026 The Network Engineer leads highly complex network infrastructure initiatives and serves as a key technical advisor to management, technical teams, vendors, and campus stakeholders on enterprise network architecture, infrastructure modernization, service reliability, security, performance, and operational standards. Temporary Hiring Pools Loading... Powered by PageUp Contact Email: hrwww@sfsu.edu Telephone: 415.338.1872 / Fax: 415.338.0521 Need Assistance? Location San Francisco State University 1600 Holloway Avenue, ADM 252 San Francisco, CA 94132 Office Hours Monday through Friday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Quick Links HR Client Support Center Calendar & Schedules FAQ's Forms SF State Gateway Accessibility Equity & Community Inclusion Environment & Sustainability Privacy Policy Title IX San Francisco State\n                            University A\n                            California State University Campus SF State Facebook SF State Twitter SF State Instagram SF State LinkedIn"
