      "title": "San Francisco State University - Details - Senior Director of Corporate and Foundation Relations (Administrator II, Range 1) - Development Office",
      "description": "San Francisco State University - Details - Senior Director of Corporate and Foundation Relations (Administrator II, Range 1) - Development Office Skip to main content SAN FRANCISCO STATE UNIVERSITY | Human Resources A–Z Calendar Login Search\n                                        SF State Search SF State Button SF State This Site Toggle navigation Menu Main navigation What's New Get Started Expand Future Employees New Employees Current Employees HR Liaisons Managers Students Jobs Benefits & Retirement Expand Overview Medical Benefits Dental Benefits Vision Benefits Retirement Services Employee Assistance Program Fee Waiver Program Voluntary Benefits & Discounts Payroll Expand Overview Payroll & Paycheck Essentials Payroll Calendar & Schedules Employment Verification Leave Accrual and Absence Management Resources Cal Employee Connect Employee Separation Clearance Process Classification & Compensation Learning & Development Expand Professional Development Performance Management Process CSU Learn Labor Relations Compliance Expand Overview Whistleblower Leaves/ Employee Accommodations/Workers' Comp Expand Leaves Program Employee Accommodations Services Workers' Compensation Resources Expand COVID-19 Employee Life Events Employee Resource Groups HR Events / Training Staff Years of Service Recognition Workplace Resources Immigration Resources CSU International Travel Expand CSU International Travel Resources CSU International Travel Guidance for Spring & Summer 2025 Community Expectations ADA: 504 and Title II Policies and Procedures Expand Policies & Procedures (Main) All Employees Faculty Management Personnel & Confidential Staff (Represented / Non-Represented) Student Employees Job Opportunities Applicant Login Job Search Filter Results Work type Management (MPP) 1 Locations Northern California San Francisco 1 Categories Appointment Type At-Will 1 Bargaining Unit MPP 1 Job Search Category/Discipline Administrative 1 Time Basis Full Time 1 Senior Director of Corporate and Foundation Relations (Administrator II, Range 1) - Development Office Apply now Job no: 560359 Work type: Management (MPP) Location: San Francisco Categories: MPP, Administrative, At-Will, Full Time Working Title Senior Director of Corporate and Foundation Relations Administrator Level (for MPP positions only) This position is an Administrator II in the California State University Management Personnel Plan (MPP), reporting to the Associate Vice President of Development. SF State University San Francisco State is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate against persons on the basis of race, religion, color, ancestry, age, disability, genetic information, gender, gender identity, gender expression, marital status, medical condition, National origin, sex, sexual orientation, covered veteran status, or any other protected status.  Reasonable accommodations will be provided for qualified applicants with disabilities who self-disclose by contacting the Senior Human Resources Manager. Applicants may visit titleix.sfsu.edu for more information on SF State's policy prohibiting discrimination, and how to file an online report using the procedures under Executive Order 1096 Revised. Inquiries can be directed to the campus Title IX Coordinator and Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Administrator by calling (415) 338-2032 or emailing vpsaem@sfsu.edu. San Francisco State is a 100% Smoke/Vapor-Free Campus.  Smoking or Vaping of any tobacco/plant-based substance is not permitted on any University properties. The person holding this position may be considered a \"mandated reporter\" under the California Child Abuse and Neglect  Reporting Act and is required to comply with the requirements set forth in CSU Executive Order 1083 as a condition of employment. This position may be a \"designated position\" in the California State University's Conflict of Interest Code.  The successful candidate accepting this position may be required to file Conflict of Interest forms subject to the regulations of the Fair Political Practices Commission. Department Development Office Appointment Type At-Will Time Base Full-Time (1.0) Work Schedule Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m Anticipated Hiring Range $11,250.00 - $12,334.00 Per Month ($135,000.00 - $148,008.00 Annually) Salary is commensurate with experience. Position Summary The Senior Director of Corporate and Foundation Relations (CFR) will build on the University-wide program to steward and grow corporate and foundation support. The University has a robust CFR fundraising presence, and the Senior Director will work to proactively expand and leverage relationships to identify and increase new funding opportunities. The Senior Director is a key member of the centralized development team and will manage the planning, organizing, and implementing of the corporate and foundation fundraising program with the goal of increasing support focused on the University’s strategic and campaign priorities. The incumbent works with senior leadership and faculty to develop and implement strategies and relationships that increase opportunities for corporate and foundation philanthropy, sponsorships, collaborative research, professional and executive training, student internships and recruitment, and continuing education. The Senior Director will have a deep understanding of both the nuances of effective foundation grant seeking and of the business and marketing needs of corporations – and the ability to develop complex relationships and strategies to address them. The senior director will implement and manage corporate and foundation relationships to facilitate communication between campus stakeholders and empower units to build deeper and broader relations with funders. The Senior Director is a self-motivated individual with proven networking and leadership skills. The Senior Director will manage the Corporate and Foundation Relations program to ensure that the mission and goals of the campus are achieved with respect to corporate and foundation support for philanthropy. The Senior Director will partner with the various colleges and major fundraising units, and their assigned development officers to provide critical resources and personnel to proactively identify funding opportunities and make fruitful matches with corporate and foundation funding sources. The Senior Director will be supported by and will manage the director of CFR in this work. This position reports to the Associate Vice President of Development. Position Information Structuring Work Develop and execute high-level comprehensive fundraising strategies for corporations and foundations with major revenue potential in support of university and campaign priorities. Develops an annual business plan based on development office and priorities in coordination with the AVP of Development. Effectively manage follow-up and reporting requirements in an appropriate manner while maintaining confidentiality. Discover and qualify new prospects, especially in the Corporate space. Plans development-oriented campus visits for current and potential partners. Inspiring Performance Lead the Corporate and Foundation Relations Office and develop strategies and plans to secure private support from corporate and foundation partners, establish goals and objectives, and measure progress against those goals/objectives. Serve as a resourceful and effective fundraising leader. Provide insight and advice to internal and external stakeholders on the opportunities of existing and potential partnership opportunities. Explore the university for corporate and foundation funding opportunities, including initiating and managing a circuit of regular presentations about CFR services to colleges, departments, and major units. Identify and promote potential sponsorship and naming opportunities throughout the campus, in close coordination with university leadership. Provide staff support to university, college and departmental leaders to help develop worthwhile funding opportunities, identify potential funders and proposals for priority programs. Building Teams Identify, develop, and manage relationships between C-level executives, board members and other corporate and foundation leaders with the University President and other senior administrators and faculty, bringing together stakeholders and establishing networks to nurture productive relationships. Arrange, manage, and prepare detailed briefs for visits and campus tours with high-level corporate and foundation leaders and the President, university leadership, and faculty. Partner with the donor relations and university communications teams to ensure the proper stewardship and acknowledgement of corporate and foundation support. Using and Sharing Information Build and manage a portfolio of active and potential corporate and foundation prospects and funders. Personally visit regularly with key corporate prospects and foundation program officers. Prepare and present written proposals for corporate and foundation funding that attract both new and current investors. Managing Talents Initiate potential funding opportunities in close coordination with deans and faculty leaders. The Senior Director manages the Director of Foundation Relations and other staff as assigned. Facilitating Change Regularly review “lapsed” corporate and foundation donors to ensure that new funding opportunities are presented to renew and/or deepen support. Professional Behavior Demonstrate behaviors that are in line with the User-Friendly Principles (P530C) and Principles of Conduct for a Multi-Cultural University (P30D) Demonstrate safe work practices for oneself, others, and the office environment. Other Duties as Assigned Minimum Qualifications • Seven or more years of successful corporate and foundation fundraising experience. • A bachelor’s degree is required; master’s degree is preferred. • Working knowledge of corporate business and foundation development settings; experience in higher ed CFR is preferred. • Proven track record of CFR solicitations and grant success. • Excellent written and oral communication skills, and experience at making presentations. Ability to synthesize information and compose thorough, clear, and effective proposals and documents. • Excellent analytical project management skills, ability to understand complex strategies, and ability to multi-task and meet competing deadlines. • Demonstrated “cold calling” experience and ability to create and sustain new relationships. • Ability to work in a diverse environment and with a diverse set of internal and external constituents. Preferred Qualifications • Understanding of the dynamics of corporate and foundation partnerships and giving, business trends, and other related business conditions that may impact corporate investments and foundation grant making. • Adaptability and sensitivity to corporate and foundation and academic objectives. Demonstrated ability to work with faculty and administrators from a variety of disciplines, and to contribute and function within a complex university setting. • Working knowledge of the Bay Area and ability to engage with the local business community. Environmental/Physical/Special • Flexibility to work on weekends, evenings, and holidays. • Automobile travel is required for visits to donors, training, and alumni events. Must possess a valid driver’s license and comply with Defensive Driver’s Training Program requirements if a vehicle is used to travel on official business. • Periodic air travel required Pre-Employment Requirements This position requires the successful completion of a background check. Eligibility to Work Applicants must be able to provide proof of US Citizenship or authorization to work in the United States, within three business days from their date of hire. Benefits Threaded through our Total Compensation package is a commitment to Bridging Life's Transitions.  SF State is committed to providing our employees with a comprehensive program that rewards efforts that are appreciated by your colleagues, students and the customers we serve. We offer a competitive compensation package that includes Medical, Dental, Vision, Pension, 401k, Healthcare Savings Account, Life Insurance, Disability Insurance, Vacation and Sick Leave as well as State Holidays and a dynamic Fee Waiver program, all geared towards the University's commitment to attract, motivate and retain our employee. CSUEU Position (For CSUEU Positions Only) Eligible and qualified on-campus applicants, currently in bargaining units 2, 5, 7, and 9 are given hiring preference. Additional Information SF STATE IS NOT A SPONSORING AGENCY FOR STAFF OR MANAGEMENT POSITIONS. (i.e. H1-B VISAS). Thank you for your interest in employment with California State University (CSU).  CSU is a state entity whose business operations reside within the State of California.  Because of this, CSU prohibits hiring employees to perform CSU-related work outside of California with very limited exception.  While this position may be eligible for occasional telework, all work is expected to be performed in the state of California, and this position is assigned to on-campus operations. CSU strongly encourages faculty, staff, and students who are accessing campus facilities to be immunized against COVID-19. The systemwide policy can be found at https://calstate.policystat.com/policy/9779821/latest/. The Human Resources office is open Mondays through Fridays from 8 a.m. to 5 p.m., and can be reached at (415) 338-1872. Please note that this position, position requirements, application deadline and/or any other component of this position is subject to change or cancellation at any time. Advertised: July 28, 2026 (9:00 AM) Pacific Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Open Date Close Date Senior Director of Corporate and Foundation Relations (Administrator II, Range 1) - Development Office San Francisco July 28, 2026 The Senior Director of Corporate and Foundation Relations (CFR) will build on the University-wide program to steward and grow corporate and foundation support. The University has a robust CFR fundraising presence, and the Senior Director will work to proactively expand and leverage relationships to identify and increase new funding opportunities. The Senior Director is a key member of the centralized development team and will manage the planning, organizing, and implementing of the corporate and foundation fundraising program with the goal of increasing support focused on the University’s strategic and campaign priorities. The incumbent works with senior leadership and faculty to develop and implement strategies and relationships that increase opportunities for corporate and foundation philanthropy, sponsorships, collaborative research, professional and executive training, student internships and recruitment, and continuing education. The senior director will implement and manage corporate and foundation relationships to facilitate communication between campus stakeholders and empower units to build deeper and broader relations with funders.  The Senior Director is a self-motivated individual with proven networking and leadership skills. The Senior Director will manage the Corporate and Foundation Relations program to ensure that the mission and goals of the campus are achieved with respect to corporate and foundation support for philanthropy. The Senior Director will partner with the various colleges and major fundraising units, and their assigned development officers to provide critical resources and personnel to proactively identify funding opportunities and make fruitful matches with corporate and foundation funding sources. The Senior Director will be supported by and will manage the director of CFR in this work. This position reports to the Associate Vice President of Development. Current opportunities Position Location Open Date Close Date Senior Director of Corporate and Foundation Relations (Administrator II, Range 1) - Development Office San Francisco July 28, 2026 The Senior Director of Corporate and Foundation Relations (CFR) will build on the University-wide program to steward and grow corporate and foundation support. The University has a robust CFR fundraising presence, and the Senior Director will work to proactively expand and leverage relationships to identify and increase new funding opportunities. The Senior Director is a key member of the centralized development team and will manage the planning, organizing, and implementing of the corporate and foundation fundraising program with the goal of increasing support focused on the University’s strategic and campaign priorities. The incumbent works with senior leadership and faculty to develop and implement strategies and relationships that increase opportunities for corporate and foundation philanthropy, sponsorships, collaborative research, professional and executive training, student internships and recruitment, and continuing education. The senior director will implement and manage corporate and foundation relationships to facilitate communication between campus stakeholders and empower units to build deeper and broader relations with funders.  The Senior Director is a self-motivated individual with proven networking and leadership skills. The Senior Director will manage the Corporate and Foundation Relations program to ensure that the mission and goals of the campus are achieved with respect to corporate and foundation support for philanthropy. The Senior Director will partner with the various colleges and