    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/873/sf/en-us/job/561711/enrollment-operations-specialist-administrative-analystspecialist-exempt-i-range-ii-cpage-administration": {
      "title": "Enrollment Operations Specialist",
      "description": "San Francisco State University - Details - Enrollment Operations Specialist - (Administrative Analyst/Specialist Exempt I, Range II) - CPAGE Administration Skip to main content SAN FRANCISCO STATE UNIVERSITY | Human Resources A–Z Calendar Login Search\n                                        SF State Search SF State Button SF State This Site Toggle navigation Menu Main navigation What's New Get Started Expand Future Employees New Employees Current Employees HR Liaisons Managers Students Jobs Benefits & Retirement Expand Overview Medical Benefits Dental Benefits Vision Benefits Retirement Services Employee Assistance Program Fee Waiver Program Voluntary Benefits & Discounts Payroll Expand Overview Payroll & Paycheck Essentials Payroll Calendar & Schedules Employment Verification Leave Accrual and Absence Management Resources Cal Employee Connect Employee Separation Clearance Process Classification & Compensation Learning & Development Expand Professional Development Performance Management Process CSU Learn Labor Relations Compliance Expand Overview Whistleblower Leaves/ Employee Accommodations/Workers' Comp Expand Leaves Program Employee Accommodations Services Workers' Compensation Resources Expand COVID-19 Employee Life Events Employee Resource Groups HR Events / Training Staff Years of Service Recognition Workplace Resources Immigration Resources CSU International Travel Expand CSU International Travel Resources CSU International Travel Guidance for Spring & Summer 2025 Community Expectations ADA: 504 and Title II Policies and Procedures Expand Policies & Procedures (Main) All Employees Faculty Management Personnel & Confidential Staff (Represented / Non-Represented) Student Employees Open Enrollment Job Opportunities Applicant Login Job Search Filter Results Work type Staff 1 Locations Northern California San Francisco 1 Categories Appointment Type Probationary 1 Bargaining Unit Unit 9 - CSUEU - Technical Support Services 1 Job Search Category/Discipline Administrative 1 Time Basis Full Time 1 Workplace Type (Exclude Inst Fac) Telecommute eligible (work onsite as scheduled and/or as requested and telecommute as scheduled) 1 Enrollment Operations Specialist - (Administrative Analyst/Specialist Exempt I, Range II) - CPAGE Administration Apply now Job no: 561711 Work type: Staff Location: San Francisco Categories: Unit 9 - CSUEU - Technical Support Services, Administrative, Probationary, Full Time, Telecommute eligible (work onsite as scheduled and/or as requested and telecommute as scheduled) *SFSU INTERNAL APPLICANTS ONLY* Working Title Enrollment Operations Specialist SF State University San Francisco State is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate against persons on the basis of race, religion, color, ancestry, age, disability, genetic information, gender, gender identity, gender expression, marital status, medical condition, National origin, sex, sexual orientation, covered veteran status, or any other protected status.  Reasonable accommodations will be provided for qualified applicants with disabilities who self-disclose by contacting the Senior Human Resources Manager. Applicants may visit titleix.sfsu.edu for more information on SF State's policy prohibiting discrimination, and how to file an online report using the procedures under Executive Order 1096 Revised. Inquiries can be directed to the campus Title IX Coordinator and Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Administrator by calling (415) 338-2032 or emailing vpsaem@sfsu.edu. San Francisco State is a 100% Smoke/Vapor-Free Campus.  Smoking or Vaping of any tobacco/plant-based substance is not permitted on any University properties. The person holding this position may be considered a \"mandated reporter\" under the California Child Abuse and Neglect  Reporting Act and is required to comply with the requirements set forth in CSU Executive Order 1083 as a condition of employment. This position may be a \"designated position\" in the California State University's Conflict of Interest Code.  The successful candidate accepting this position may be required to file Conflict of Interest forms subject to the regulations of the Fair Political Practices Commission. Department College of Professional & Global Education Appointment Type This is a one year probationary position. Time Base Full Time (1.0 FTE) Work Schedule Monday through Friday, from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Anticipated Hiring Range $5,274.000 - $5,709.00 monthly ($63,288.00 - $68,508.00 annually) Salary is commensurate with experience. Position Summary The Enrollment Operations Specialist (EOS) performs independent professional analytical work to evaluate, improve, and support Enrollment Services operations. The EOS analyzes enrollment processes and data, identifies operational risks and inefficiencies, develops and implements business process improvements, and applies functional expertise to enrollment operations. Reporting to the Director of Enrollment Services, the EOS independently interprets university, CSU, and CPaGE policies and determines their operational application in complex or unique situations. The position develops recommendations for management, exercises independent judgment in resolving operational issues, and leads or contributes to enrollment-related process improvement and system initiatives from planning through implementation and assessment. The position combines analytical responsibility, functional expertise, hands-on enrollment operations, and a strong customer service orientation to ensure accurate, responsive, and compliant enrollment services. The EOS identifies opportunities to improve services and processes and enhance the student experience while maintaining compliance with university, CSU, and regulatory requirements. Position Information Operational Analysis, Process Improvement & Systems Independently evaluate enrollment operations, workflows, and business processes to identify operational risks, inefficiencies, service gaps, and opportunities for improvement. Develop, recommend, document, and implement new or revised business processes, procedures, and standard operating procedures; assess results and make further adjustments as needed. Conduct operational and data analyses, prepare reports, identify trends or issues, and develop recommendations for management that inform departmental decisions and priorities. Lead enrollment-related operational initiatives and process improvement projects, including planning, coordinating implementation, monitoring progress, and assessing outcomes. Apply Enrollment Services functional expertise to the testing, implementation, and adoption of enrollment-related technologies and system changes; evaluate operational impacts and recommend business process changes. Consult with the Director of Enrollment Services and campus partners on operational issues and recommend solutions that balance policy, service, compliance, and departmental needs. Enrollment Operations & Functional Expertise Perform individual and high-volume staff-assisted enrollment and registration transactions, including batch or cohort enrollments, for populations that cannot enroll through standard self-service processes, including closed or restricted courses and designated student populations. Process adds, drops, withdrawals, refunds, petitions, and other enrollment transactions and maintain accurate student records in Campus Solutions and related systems. Research and evaluate enrollment exceptions or complex cases that cannot be addressed through standard procedures; apply functional expertise to interpret applicable university, CSU, and CPaGE policies and system requirements, determine the appropriate resolution, and document decisions as needed. Exercise independent judgment and delegated decision-making within the scope of the position to resolve complex enrollment and student record issues that are not fully addressed by established procedures. Coordinate with CPaGE program team, academic departments, Financial Aid, Bursar, Registrar, and other campus offices to research and resolve cross-functional enrollment issues, including cases requiring evaluation of enrollment eligibility, payment status, or other administrative requirements. Monitor high-volume registration and enrollment periods, identify emerging operational issues, and independently develop or recommend corrective actions to ensure continuity of service. Maintain functional knowledge of Campus Solutions and other university systems and identify system or process issues affecting the accuracy and integrity of student records. Student, Faculty & Campus Consultation Provide consultation and guidance to students, faculty, program coordinators, and campus partners on complex enrollment matters, policies, procedures, and operational requirements. Research and resolve complex student and partner issues requiring analysis and coordination across multiple departments. Explain policy determinations and operational decisions clearly and recommend appropriate options or next steps based on the circumstances of each case. Build collaborative relationships with campus partners to identify recurring issues, evaluate their operational impact, and develop sustainable solutions. Share functional expertise and cross-train staff on enrollment processes, policy application, system functionality, and revised procedures. Participate on cross-functional committees and workgroups, contributing Enrollment Services functional expertise. Identify patterns in inquiries and service issues and recommend changes to communications, procedures, or systems to improve the student and partner experience. Lead or contribute to special analytical and operational projects that support Enrollment Services, CPaGE, and SFSU priorities. Perform other related duties consistent with the scope and level of the position. Demonstrate behaviors that are in line with the User Friendly Principles (P530C) and Principles of Conduct for a Multi-Cultural University (P30D). Demonstrate safe work practices for oneself, others, and the office environment. Other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Thorough knowledge of administrative operations, business processes, and analytical methods in a complex organizational environment. Ability to independently interpret and apply university, CSU, and CPaGE policies and regulations and determine appropriate operational application in complex or unique situations. Demonstrated ability to independently analyze complex operational problems, evaluate alternatives, exercise sound judgment, and make or recommend decisions with significant operational impact. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, including the ability to gather and evaluate data, identify trends and risks, develop recommendations, and assess the effectiveness of implemented solutions. Ability to develop, recommend, implement, document, and evaluate business processes, procedures, and operational improvements. Ability to plan and lead operational initiatives, system implementations, and process improvement projects involving multiple stakeholders. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills, including the ability to present analyses and recommendations and build collaborative working relationships with students, faculty, staff, and campus partners. Ability to serve as a functional subject matter expert and provide consultation, guidance, and training to others on enrollment operations, policy application Experience Equivalent to two years of progressively responsible professional experience in enrollment, student services, administrative operations, or a related functional area involving independent analysis, policy interpretation, development of recommendations, process improvement, and decision-making responsibility. Education Equivalent to graduation from a four-year college or university in business administration, public administration, higher education, communications, or a related field. Additional qualifying experience ma be substituted for the required education on a year-for-year basis. Preferred Qualifications Experience independently analyzing enrollment, registration, admissions, student records, or related administrative operations in a college or university environment. Experience using Campus Solutions, PeopleSoft, Salesforce, or other enterprise student information or customer relationship management systems. Experience supporting Professional & Continuing Education or Extended Education programs. Experience developing, recommending, implementing, and evaluating business processes and standard operating procedures. Strong proficiency with Microsoft Excel and other productivity software, including experience analyzing operational data and preparing reports or recommendations for management. Experience leading or coordinating system implementations, operational initiatives, or process improvement projects. Knowledge of California State University and San Francisco State University policies and procedures. Environmental/Physical/Special Must be able to work for extended periods at a computer workstation and interact frequently with students, faculty, staff, and external constituents through a variety of communication methods. The position requires sustained attention to detail while managing multiple priorities during periods of high enrollment activity. May occasionally be required to move materials weighing up to 45 pounds. Must be able to work effectively with a diverse campus community while maintaining professionalism in a fast-paced, high-visibility. Pre-Employment Requirements This position requires the successful completion of a background check. Eligibility to Work Applicants must be able to provide proof of US Citizenship or authorization to work in the United States, within three business days from their date of hire. Benefits Threaded through our Total Compensation package is a commitment to Bridging Life's Transitions.  SF State is committed to providing our employees with a comprehensive program that rewards efforts that are appreciated by your colleagues, students and the customers we serve. We offer a competitive compensation package that includes Medical, Dental, Vision, Pension, 401k, Healthcare Savings Account, Life Insurance, Disability Insurance, Vacation and Sick Leave as well as State Holidays and a dynamic Fee Waiver program, all geared towards the University's commitment to attract, motivate and retain our employee. CSUEU Position (For CSUEU Positions Only) Eligible and qualified on-campus applicants, currently in bargaining units 2, 5, 7, and 9 are given hiring preference. Additional Information SF STATE IS NOT A SPONSORING AGENCY FOR STAFF OR MANAGEMENT POSITIONS. (i.e. H1-B VISAS). Thank you for your interest in employment with California State University (CSU).  CSU is a state entity whose business operations reside within the State of California.  Because of this, CSU prohibits hiring employees to perform CSU-related work outside of California with very limited exception.  While this position may be eligible for occasional telework, all work is expected to be performed in the state of California, and this position is assigned to on-campus operations. CSU strongly encourages faculty, staff, and students who are accessing campus facilities to be immunized against COVID-19. The systemwide policy can be found at https://calstate.policystat.com/policy/9779821/latest/. The Human Resources office is open Mondays through Fridays from 8 a.m. to 5 p.m., and can be reached at (415) 338-1872. Please note that this position, position requirements, application deadline and/or any other component of this position is subject to change or cancellation at any time. *SFSU INTERNAL APPLICANTS ONLY* Advertised: September 10, 2026 (9:00 AM) Pacific Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Open Date Close Date Enrollment Operations Specialist - (Administrative Analyst/Specialist Exempt I, Range II) - CPAGE Administration San Francisco September 10, 2026 The Enrollment Operations Specialist (EOS) performs independent professional analytical work to evaluate, improve, and support Enrollment Services operations. The EOS analyzes enrollment processes and data, identifies operational risks and inefficiencies, develops and implements business process improvements, and applies functional expertise to enrollment operations.\nReporting to the Director of Enrollment Services, the EOS independently interprets university, CSU, and CPaGE policies and determines their operational application in complex or unique situations. The position develops recommendations for management, exercises independent judgment in resolving operational issues, and leads or contributes to enrollment-related process improvement and system initiatives from planning through implementation and assessment.\nThe position combines analytical responsibility, functional expertise, hands-on enrollment operations, and a strong customer service orientation to ensure accurate, responsive, and compliant enrollment services. The EOS identifies opportunities to improve services and processes and enhance the student experience while maintaining compliance with university, CSU, and regulatory requirements. Current opportunities Position Location Open Date Close Date Enrollment Operations Specialist - (Administrative Analyst/Specialist Exempt I, Range II) - CPAGE Administration San Francisco September 10, 2026 The Enrollment Operations Specialist (EOS) performs independent professional analytical work to evaluate, improve, and support Enrollment Services operations. The EOS analyzes enrollment processes and data, identifies operational risks and inefficiencies, develops and implements business process improvements, and applies functional expertise to enrollment operations.\nReporting to the Director of Enrollment Services, the EOS independently interprets university, CSU, and CPaGE policies and determines their operational application in complex or unique situations. The position develops recommendations for management, exercises independent judgment in resolving operational issues, and leads or contributes to enrollment-related process improvement and system initiatives from planning through implementation and assessment.\nThe position combines analytical responsibility, functional expertise, hands-on enrollment operations, and a strong customer service orientation to ensure accurate, responsive, and compliant enrollment services. The EOS identifies opportunities to improve services and processes and enhance the student experience while maintaining compliance with university, CSU, and regulatory requirements. Temporary Hiring Pools Loading... Powered by PageUp Contact Email: hrwww@sfsu.edu Telephone: 415.338.1872 / Fax: 415.338.0521 Need Assistance? Location San Francisco State University 1600 Holloway Avenue, ADM 252 San Francisco, CA 94132 Office Hours Monday through Friday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Quick Links HR Client Support Center Calendar & Schedules FAQ's Forms SF State Gateway Accessibility Equity & Community Inclusion Environment & Sustainability Privacy Policy Title IX San Francisco State\n                            University A\n                            California State University Campus SF State Facebook SF State Twitter SF State Instagram SF State LinkedIn"
